# Language

Read `CONTEXT.md` before naming a domain concept. Use glossary terms exactly.

When two words mean the same thing, pick the glossary word. List the other under `_Avoid_` in `CONTEXT.md` — then stop using it.

```md
**Invoice**:
A request for payment sent to a customer after delivery.
_Avoid_: Bill, payment request
```

Say `Invoice`, not `Bill`. General programming words (timeout, handler, queue) stay out of the glossary.
